      },
      "lineNbr": 76,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-01T12:40:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we separate this into a helper function so that early returns can be used to simplify control flow a bit potentially?",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "174523d0_53536b88",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-01T12:40:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a link to documentation that explains this? It seems non-obvious even for UMA system because there might be pagetable stuff that could make this not true.",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3dac9435_a7208efe",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-02T17:45:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just to be clear, are *we* defining CUSTOM heap this way, or is something external (d3d12 or driver or chromium?) define it this way?\n\nIn general I\u0027m a bit confused about the high level logic here so a high level comment would be helpful. For example why do we branch on `isUMA` instead of some driver-reported info for this specific heap from `heapProperties`? `isUMA` seems possibly too broad. (Maybe this is the same as Corentin\u0027s comment.)",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c224ca2_4c4b60ee",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 98,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-02T22:17:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe that https://microsoft.github.io/DirectX-Specs/d3d/D3D12GPUUploadHeaps.html explains it. I\u0027m just following the specification for READBACK/UPLOAD/DEFAULT and ignoring GPU_UPLOAD. I\u0027ll add a table in the comments and cite that link.",
      "parentUuid": "174523d0_53536b88",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3a21d69_0c284c55",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-01T12:40:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If possible, I\u0027d rather avoid adding MapWrite here because there is no way for Dawn to ensure that the application won\u0027t read the mapped memory, which would be insanely slow in this mode.",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e99cdb40_edb4f4a2",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000861
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-02T22:17:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that L0 + WRITE_COMBINE is equivalent to UPLOAD heaps on non ccUMA architectures. We use [d3d12_device_-\u003eGetCustomHeapProperties(0, D3D12_HEAP_TYPE_UPLOAD)](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:gpu/command_buffer/service/shared_image/d3d_image_backing_factory.cc;l\u003d824;drc\u003d9b4c9ad003587ffb6878dd7e3aa7f83c07d7747d) in shared image. That said, we don\u0027t currently have a use-case for MapAsync from WebGPU. WebNN can always WriteTensor/ReadTensor to/from these resources (even if it would be slow).",
      "parentUuid": "d3a21d69_0c284c55",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e391301a_ce198f14",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 118,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-01T12:40:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is `MapWrite` added only when `isCacheCoherent`? It would be slower then if it were cache coherent, but wouldn\u0027t it always be faster than doing an intermediate copy?",
      "revId": "00e3f1a8b9c9dfaf2c3e5e513a76d34d1fb3edcc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e4aef370_59667cfb",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/SharedBufferMemoryD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 118,
